<title>GERMANY: Thyssen 1995/96 profit 350 mln DM.</title>
<headline>Thyssen 1995/96 profit 350 mln DM.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30 (in</p>
<p>millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   350  vs     775</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     654  vs   1,026</p>
<p>    Group sales			     38,700  vs  39,100</p>
<p>    Dividend					 8  vs	10 marks</p>
<p>    Investment				 2,400  vs   2,200</p>
<p>    Cash flow				  2,200  vs   2,800</p>
<p>    Group workforce (on Sept 30)     122,659  vs 126,444</p>
<p>NOTE - Thyssen AG said its steel division sales were 10.6 billion marks, and that the division profit was considerable lower than the year before. Capital goods sales rose to 12.7 billion marks and profit was generally higher. The trade and services division saw sales of 18.2 billion marks, just below the previous year's level, but profit was down sharply.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
